Subject: [PATCH 10/10] =?UTF-8?q?fix(input):=20own=20multi-finger=20touch?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20sequences=20=E2=80=94=20gestures=20stop=20leaking=20to=20app?=
 =?UTF-8?q?s?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two bugs made app-level interactions fire during our gestures:

1. TouchSwipeGrab "swallowed" by passing a null focus through to
   TouchInnerHandle::motion — but smithay's TouchInternal::motion ignores
   that argument entirely and delivers to the focus recorded at down
   time. Every motion of an animated or discrete gesture kept streaming
   to the surface under the fingers: browsers pinch-zoomed from 3-finger
   swipes, terminals drag-selected and touch-scrolled under hold-swipes.

2. Ending those touches via TouchHandle::cancel() does not work:
   TouchInternal::cancel skips any slot whose events were already
   frame-flushed — which is all of them, since every event is followed
   by a frame. It sends nothing and clears nothing.

The fix, in three parts:

- Ownership: once enough fingers for a touchscreen gesture are down
  (touchscreen-swipe.fingers, gestures enabled, no other grab active),
  niri latches touch_input_suspended, ends the touches the client has
  already seen with synthetic up events plus a frame — a clean, universal
  end for in-progress app gestures — and stops delivering down/motion/up
  until the last finger lifts (tracker back to idle). The single-finger
  edge tracker is reset so it cannot fire mid-sequence.

- TouchSwipeGrab now swallows for real: the down/up/motion pass-through
  calls are gone; the grab feeds only its own tracker. When a gesture
  grab installs at recognition the suspension clears, because the grab
  receives events via the normal dispatch and no longer forwards them.

- The edge-swipe install ends its initiating finger the same way
  (synthetic up) before the swallow grab takes over; previously that
  touch stayed outstanding on the client forever.

Gesture behavior is unchanged — taps, flicks, hold-swipes and the
animated swipes run exactly as before. Single- and two-finger input
(including app pinch-zoom) is untouched. Escape hatch for apps needing
N-finger touches: raise touchscreen-swipe.fingers.
